# Ship the self-test inside the sdist.
#
# SECURITY.md tells people to reproduce a suspected bug against
# ``tests/mock_relay.py`` rather than paste a real report. That instruction is
# only useful if the mock relay is actually in the archive, and setuptools does
# not pick up tests/ or examples/ on its own.
include LICENSE
include README.md
include README.en.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include SECURITY.md
# Not needed to build, but the sdist carries every root document so the archive
# is self-describing: someone reading a copy of the source should be able to see
# how a release is cut without going back to the repository.
include RELEASING.md
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include examples *.md
# The Windows desktop build is source, not package data: it is not importable and
# nothing in relaycheck/ touches it. It rides along so that someone with only the
# sdist can still build the exe instead of cloning the repository.
#
# *.ico / *.png are load-bearing here, not decoration. relaycheck_gui.spec points
# `icon=` and `datas=` straight at gui/relaycheck.ico and gui/relaycheck.png, and
# PyInstaller raises FileNotFoundError — after doing all the expensive analysis —
# when an icon path does not exist. Omitting them does not produce an icon-less
# exe; it produces no exe at all, which is how 0.1.4's sdist shipped.
recursive-include gui *.py *.ps1 *.spec *.md *.ico *.png
